# integration.rts_api_play: a select-and-attack and a camera scroll, pushed through SDL's queue.
#
# Coordinates are the view's (1280 by 720); `aim` puts the pointer where the game's camera shows a
# unit now, as a person's eyes would.
0   move 640 360
# A box dragged round the far three columns of blue's swordsmen (units 2, 3, 4, 7, 8 and 9): the
# camera looks east, so the field's x runs up the screen and its z to the right.
20  aim unit 2 -16 16
21  press left
24  aim unit 6 0 0
27  aim unit 9 16 -16
30  release left
# A right click on red's first swordsman: every selected unit is ordered to attack it.
40  aim unit 24
42  press right
44  release right
# The keyboard pan: D held for half a second slides the camera to its right, the pointer in the
# middle of the view so no screen edge pans it too.
50  move 640 360
60  key d down
90  key d up
